  "result": {
    "summary": "The fix changes the auto-handover notice in orchestrator/planner_context.py to contain 'write the checkpoint', 'compacts in place' and '--session-id S'. These are the three strings tests/test_cli.py asserts, so the failing test_handover_cli_forwards_session_id should now pass. I did not run the test suite. The notice stays one line. The once-per-100k-band logic is unchanged, and nothing under .claude/hooks is touched. The test helper _started was updated to take the session id, and the two session-specific assertions now pass 'other'.",
